message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "SiteWindow: site-energy landscapes and deliverable-capacity limits for hydrogen storage in defect-engineered sp2 carbon"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Gupta
    given-names: Avin
    affiliation: "University of North Texas"
keywords:
  - hydrogen storage
  - carbon nanomaterials
  - graphene
  - carbon nanotubes
  - defect engineering
  - adsorption
  - chemisorption
  - deliverable capacity
  - electron irradiation
  - uncertainty quantification
abstract: >-
  SiteWindow constructs, calibrates and evaluates the landscape of hydrogen binding sites in
  defective, curved and oxygen-functionalized sp2 carbon against the thermodynamic, kinetic and
  stoichiometric constraints of a storage cycle, including a window theory of deliverable
  capacity with a variational bound, multi-fidelity atomistic workflows, electron knock-on and
  defect-population models with Raman observables, forward thermal-desorption models, and
  inference of adsorption-energy distributions from the public NIST/ARPA-E isotherm corpus.
